### ============================================================================
### SIS 1 — Online Store REST API HTTP Client Collection (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### ============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### 0. Check Active Maven Profile & AppProperties (Week 2) — 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/config
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================================
### 1. CATEGORIES (/api/v1/categories)
### ============================================================================

### 1.1 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Get all categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories
Accept: application/json

### 1.2 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Get category by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/1
Accept: application/json

### 1.3 [ERROR 404 Not Found] Get non-existent category
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/999
Accept: application/json

### 1.4 [SUCCESS 201 Created + Location] Create a new category
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gaming Consoles",
  "description": "PlayStation, Xbox, and Nintendo consoles"
}

### 1.5 [ERROR 400 Bad Request] Create category — Bean Validation failure (blank name)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "description": "Invalid category with blank name"
}

### 1.6 [ERROR 409 Conflict] Create category — Duplicate category name
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Laptops",
  "description": "Duplicate category name should return 409 Conflict"
}

### 1.7 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Update category by ID (id=4 created in step 1.4)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/categories/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Consoles & VR",
  "description": "Next-gen consoles and virtual reality headsets"
}

### 1.8 [ERROR 409 Conflict] Delete category that still contains products (id=1)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/1

### 1.9 [SUCCESS 204 No Content] Delete empty category (id=4)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/4


### ============================================================================
### 2. PRODUCTS (/api/v1/products)
### ============================================================================

### 2.1 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Get all products
GET {{baseUrl}}/products
Accept: application/json

### 2.2 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Get products filtered by categoryId=1
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?categoryId=1
Accept: application/json

### 2.3 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Get product by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/1
Accept: application/json

### 2.4 [ERROR 404 Not Found] Get non-existent product
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/999
Accept: application/json

### 2.5 [SUCCESS 201 Created + Location] Create a new product
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAPTOP-002",
  "name": "ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16",
  "description": "Gaming laptop with RTX 4070 and OLED display",
  "price": 1799.99,
  "stockQuantity": 15,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 2.6 [ERROR 400 Bad Request] Create product — Bean Validation failure (invalid SKU, negative price)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "bad sku!",
  "name": "A",
  "description": "Invalid fields",
  "price": -50.00,
  "stockQuantity": -1,
  "categoryId": null
}

### 2.7 [ERROR 409 Conflict] Create product — Duplicate SKU
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAPTOP-001",
  "name": "Duplicate SKU Laptop",
  "description": "Should fail with 409 Conflict",
  "price": 1200.00,
  "stockQuantity": 5,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 2.8 [ERROR 404 Not Found] Create product — Non-existent categoryId
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAPTOP-099",
  "name": "Orphan Laptop",
  "description": "Category 999 does not exist",
  "price": 1200.00,
  "stockQuantity": 5,
  "categoryId": 999
}

### 2.9 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Update product (id=4)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAPTOP-002",
  "name": "ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16 (2026 Edition)",
  "description": "Updated gaming laptop",
  "price": 1699.99,
  "stockQuantity": 20,
  "categoryId": 1
}

### 2.10 [SUCCESS 204 No Content] Delete product (id=4)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/4


### ============================================================================
### 3. ORDERS (/api/v1/orders)
### ============================================================================

### 3.1 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Get all orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Accept: application/json

### 3.2 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Get order by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/1
Accept: application/json

### 3.3 [ERROR 404 Not Found] Get non-existent order
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/999
Accept: application/json

### 3.4 [SUCCESS 201 Created + Location] Create a new order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Dana Akhmetova",
  "customerEmail": "dana@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": 2,
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### 3.5 [ERROR 400 Bad Request] Create order — Bean Validation failure (invalid email & quantity=0)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "",
  "customerEmail": "not-an-email",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": 1,
      "quantity": 0
    }
  ]
}

### 3.6 [ERROR 409 Conflict] Create order — Insufficient stock
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Bulk Buyer",
  "customerEmail": "buyer@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": 1,
      "quantity": 95
    }
  ]
}

### 3.7 [SUCCESS 200 OK] Update order status to DELIVERED (id=2)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/orders/2/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DELIVERED"
}

### 3.8 [ERROR 409 Conflict] Update status of already DELIVERED order (id=2)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/orders/2/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CANCELLED"
}

### 3.9 [SUCCESS 204 No Content] Delete order (id=1)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/orders/1
